export default {"id":"bassstation-level-14","number":14,"title":"Arpeggiator Architecture & Performance Engine","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"- Master the real-time operation of the Arpeggiator controls: On, Latch, Tempo, Rhythm, Mode, Octaves, and Swing. - Understand the clock priority hierarchy, external MIDI clock synchronization, and the automatic Flywheel tempo buffer.","modules":[{"id":"bassstation-m-14-1","code":"14","title":"Arpeggiator Architecture & Performance Engine","blurb":"- Master the real-time operation of the Arpeggiator controls: On, Latch, Tempo, Rhythm, Mode, Octaves, and Swing. - Understand the clock priority hierarchy, external MIDI clock synchronization, and the automatic Flywheel tempo buffer.","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"bassstation-l-o-14","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Section 14.1 — Real-Time Pattern Generation & Clock Dynamics","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Section Learning Outcomes","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Master the real-time operation of the Arpeggiator controls: <strong>On</strong>, <strong>Latch</strong>, <strong>Tempo</strong>, <strong>Rhythm</strong>, <strong>Mode</strong>, <strong>Octaves</strong>, and <strong>Swing</strong>.","Understand the clock priority hierarchy, external MIDI clock synchronization, and the automatic <strong>Flywheel</strong> tempo buffer.","Analyze and apply the complete arpeggiator playback modes: <strong>Up</strong>, <strong>Down</strong>, <strong>UpDn</strong>, <strong>UpDn2</strong>, <strong>Played</strong>, and <strong>Random</strong>.","Program micro-timing groove using the On-Key <strong>Swing</strong> parameter (1% to 99%).","Utilize the <strong>Key Hold</strong> drone functionality when the arpeggiator engine is powered off."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-14-1-1","title":"14.1.1: Arpeggiator Activation and Latch States","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The Arpeggiator decomposes held musical chords into sequential rhythmic single-note patterns:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                      ARPEGGIATOR CONTROL STATE MAP\n   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │ [On Button]    ──► Enables / Disables Arpeggiator (LED On)  │\n   │ [Latch Button] ──► Retains active pattern after keys released│\n   │                                                             │\n   │ *Pre-Latch Memory Gesture*:                                 │\n   │ Pressing [Latch] BEFORE pressing [On] uses the LAST held    │\n   │ chord stored in memory to launch the arpeggio instantly.    │\n   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Standard Latch</strong>:","Hold down a chord and press <strong>Latch</strong>.","You can release your hands from the keybed; the arpeggio continues playing indefinitely. Striking a new chord replaces the latched pattern.","<strong>Pre-Latch Memory Recall</strong>:","If you play a chord, release it, and subsequently press <strong>Latch</strong> followed by <strong>On</strong>, the microprocessor recalls the last held chord buffer and launches the pattern immediately."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-14-1-2","title":"14.1.2: Internal Tempo (40–240 BPM), External MIDI Clock, and Flywheel","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Internal Clock</strong>:","The <strong>Tempo</strong> rotary potentiometer adjusts internal clock speed from <strong>40 BPM to 240 BPM</strong>.","The 3-character display temporarily shows the exact numerical BPM when the knob is turned.","<strong>External MIDI Clock Takeover</strong>:","When the Bass Station II receives external MIDI Clock (via USB or 5-Pin DIN IN) from a host DAW or master drum machine, <strong>the external clock automatically overrides the internal tempo</strong>.","The physical <strong>Tempo</strong> knob is temporarily deactivated.","<strong>The Flywheel Resilience Architecture</strong>:","If external MIDI clock is suddenly disconnected or stopped during a live performance, the Bass Station II does not abruptly stop.","It seamlessly engages its <strong>Flywheel buffer</strong>, continuing playback at the last-known incoming external BPM until the user physically rotates the <strong>Tempo</strong> knob to re-establish manual internal tempo control."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Hardware Verification & Practical Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Turn Arp <strong>On</strong> and rotate the <strong>Tempo</strong> knob; verify that the display indicates exact BPM from 40 to 240.","Connect USB to a DAW sending 130 BPM MIDI clock; verify playback locks to 130 BPM.","Stop DAW playback; verify the synthesizer continues playing smoothly at 130 BPM via the Flywheel engine."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-14-1-3","title":"14.1.3: The 32 Rhythmic Patterns (Rhythm 1–32)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The <strong>Rhythm</strong> rotary switch selects one of <strong>32 pre-programmed rhythmic velocity and timing templates</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    RHYTHMIC PATTERN CLASSIFICATION                         │\n├───────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Pattern Range │ Rhythmic Character &amp; Velocity Dynamic                      │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Rhythm `1`    │ Straight continuous crotchets / eighth notes (100% steady) │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Rhythm `2–10` │ Basic syncopated grooves, dotted accents &amp; dynamic rests   │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Rhythm `11–24`│ Complex polyrhythmic grooves, funk syncopations &amp; swings   │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Rhythm `25–32`│ Extreme syncopated, broken-beat &amp; experimental accents     │\n└───────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Pattern complexity and dynamic velocity variation increase progressively as you advance from <code>1</code> to <code>32</code>."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-14-1-4","title":"14.1.4: Arpeggiator Playback Modes","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The <strong>Mode</strong> rotary switch selects the directional traversal algorithm through held chord notes:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                         ARPEGGIATOR MODE MATRIX                            │\n├───────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Mode          │ Note Traversal Order                                       │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ `Up`          │ Lowest pitch to highest pitch sequentially.                │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ `Down`        │ Highest pitch to lowest pitch sequentially.                │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ `UpDn`        │ Up then Down (Repeats lowest and highest boundary notes).  │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ `UpDn2`       │ Up then Down WITHOUT repeating boundary notes (Smooth).    │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ `Played`      │ Exact chronological order in which keys were struck.       │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ `Random`      │ True pseudorandom selection across all held pitches.       │\n└───────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>(Note: The <code>Record</code> and <code>Play</code> positions on the Mode rotary are dedicated exclusively to the 32-Step Sequencer).</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Hardware Verification & Practical Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Hold a 4-note chord (C-E-G-B).","Switch Mode between <strong>UpDn</strong> and <strong>UpDn2</strong>; listen to how UpDn repeats the top <code>B</code> and bottom <code>C</code>, while UpDn2 bounces cleanly without note duplication.","Switch to <strong>Played</strong>; strike notes in non-standard order (G, then C, then B, then E); verify the arpeggio loops the exact strike sequence."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-14-1-5","title":"14.1.5: Octave Multiplication (Octaves 1–4)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The <strong>Octaves</strong> control multiplies the range of the arpeggiator across <strong>1, 2, 3, or 4 octaves</strong>:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong><code>1</code></strong>: Pattern plays strictly within the physical keybed octave range of the held keys.","<strong><code>2</code></strong>: Pattern plays held notes, then shifts the entire pattern +1 octave up before cycling.","<strong><code>3</code> or <code>4</code></strong>: Expands the arpeggio across 3 or 4 sequential ascending octaves, dramatically multiplying overall sequence length."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-14-1-6","title":"14.1.6: Micro-Timing Swing (1% to 99%)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Groove Symmetrization</strong>:","Sets the timing relationship between even and odd rhythmic steps.","<strong><code>50%</code> (Default)</strong>: Perfect mathematical straight timing (even grid).","<strong><code>51%</code> to <code>99%</code></strong>: Shuffles/swings the groove by delaying even-numbered 16th notes (classic triplet bounce, MPC swing).","<strong><code>1%</code> to <code>49%</code></strong>: Early swing/push (anti-swing rush).","<strong>On-Key Activation</strong>:","Press <strong>Function / Exit</strong>, then press the <strong>Arp Swing</strong> key (the upper <code>F#</code> key).","Display indicates <code>1</code> to <code>99</code>. Adjust using <strong>Patch/Value ▲ and ▼</strong>."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-14-1-7","title":"14.1.7: Key Hold Drone Operation","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.7: Key Hold Drone Operation","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"1. Technical Exposition","level":4},{"type":"prose","html":"When the Arpeggiator <strong>On</strong> button is turned <strong>OFF</strong>, the <strong>Latch / Rest</strong> button transforms into a <strong>Key Hold (Drone)</strong> latch:"},{"type":"list","items":["Ensure Arp <strong>On</strong> is disabled (LED off).","Strike a key or bass note and press <strong>Latch</strong>.","Release the key; the note sustains indefinitely through the Amp Envelope sustain stage, creating a continuous synthesizer drone for tuning, filter sweeping, or external audio processing."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Assessment Gate H — Self-Assessment Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Before advancing to Module 15, verify complete mastery of Gate H proficiencies:"},{"type":"list","items":["[ ] <strong>Arp &amp; Latch Operation</strong>: Launch an arpeggio, engage Latch, and change chord roots in real time.","[ ] <strong>Tempo &amp; Flywheel</strong>: Explain internal BPM adjustment range and demonstrate the Flywheel fallback when external MIDI clock stops.","[ ] <strong>Mode &amp; Octave Range</strong>: Demonstrate Up, Down, UpDn2, and Random modes across a 3-octave span.","[ ] <strong>Swing Programming</strong>: Access the On-Key Swing menu and adjust swing from 50% to 66% (triplet shuffle).","[ ] <strong>Key Hold Engagement</strong>: Demonstrate engaging a sustained drone using the Latch button with the arpeggiator powered off."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
